  "question": {
    "text": "Complex <math> <mtext>X</mtext> </math> of composition <math><mtext>Cr</mtext><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>C</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>l</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msub></math> has a spin only magnetic moment of <math> <mrow> <mtext>3</mtext><mtext>.83</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>BM</mtext></mrow> </math>. It reacts with <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mtext>N</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> and shows geometrical isomerism. The IUPAC nomenclature of <math> <mtext>X</mtext> </math> is",
