  "solution": {
    "text": "This compound can be identified and named as follows<br /><math><mtext>Cr</mtext><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>C</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>l</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msub></math><br />As <math><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>complex</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3.8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt></math><br />On solving <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br />Oxidation No. of <math> <mrow> <mtext>Cr</mtext><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow> </math><br>As compound also shows Geometrical isomerism so it will be <math><mo>[</mo><mtext>Cr</mtext><mfenced close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>C</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>l</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mtext>Cl</mtext><mo>.</mo><mtext>2</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math><br />It is named as <math><mo>→</mo></math> Tetraaquadichloridochromium(III)chloride dihydrate",
